{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form","id":489160,"title":"Devil Inside (Tell) = unlimited access to Dalu form?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T02:07:36-07:00","id":489160,"title":"Devil Inside (Tell) = unlimited access to Dalu form?","content":"In a somewhat ambiguous case of <i>Cursed with Awesome</i>, what prevents a Wolf-Blooded human with the <b>Devil Inside</b> Tell from staying inconspicuously stuck in Dalu form, and enjoy all the benefits (and drawbacks, I guess) of that form when, I don't know, being made to wear a Crucifix, wear a religious talisman or even a religious-themed t-shirt (<a href=\"http://www.helsinki.fi/~pjojala/Illegal_Christian_T-Shirt_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.helsinki.fi/~pjojala/Ille..._T-Shirt_2.jpg</a>).<br /> <br /> I mean, it doesn't take a very crafty or devilish player to read that Tell that and think of the possibilities. At the very least, a teammate could be asked to carry the symbol and trigger the transformation for you, and remove the symbol when it's no longer needed. Of course, one could argue the meaning of &quot;presented forcefully&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's still not full werewolf status, by far, but since Tells can explicitly (p.300, under Changes) be kept when one becomes any other supernatural creature, it's an obvious perk (though sometimes... an inconvenience).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 04-23-2015, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T04:31:34-07:00","id":489282,"title":"","content":"I would rule it only works when the religious symbol is presented antagonistically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T05:37:54-07:00","id":489360,"title":"","content":"*Tosses packmate a cross* &quot;Here, brandish this at me.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really see a problem. Yeah, they can transform at will. But they will also transform at not-will under what is a pretty broad set of situations. A lot of other tells have bennies that outweigh the problems, really. Like the one that gives you armour at the cost of looking kinda freaky when you get cut. Exploit away, I say!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:08:28-07:00","id":489495,"title":"","content":"Little Old Lady: &quot;Good day, youngster. Have you heard the word of the Lord?&quot; ::gives youngster religious pamphlet::<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded/Former Wolf-blooded: ::blinks and shifts to Dalu::<br /> <br /> Little Old Lady: ::succumbs to Lunacy, falls into a gibbering mass::<br /> <br /> <br /> Nope, seems totally legit to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:44:37-07:00","id":489609,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the biggest draw back would be the Lunacy, not only is it likely to inform the herd, but it's kind of rude to go around potentially damaging people's mental health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:54:16-07:00","id":489617,"title":"","content":"Or you know, consigning them to Hisil the next time they dramatically fail if they get Receptive Lunacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T06:56:59-07:00","id":490491,"title":"","content":"OK, for one moment, imagine the character was forcefully tatooed a religious symbol: would the drawbacks balance with the benefits of being a Badass Motherfucker all the time? I'm talking from a game balance perspective, for I find the idea thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:47:10-07:00","id":490545,"title":"","content":"Let me preface my statement by saying that I'm an Exalted player. I favor awesome over rules every time. I find permanently Dalu tattooed guy to be awesome, and it's totally legit in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:52:11-07:00","id":490549,"title":"","content":"It says &quot;until he leaves the scene&quot; though. It doesn't say he can't take the thing that set him off with him. <br /> <br /> Also at what point does a tattoo count as a religious symbol? And would the sudden shapeshifting that occurs at that point potentially ruin the picture? <br /> <br /> And does carving the symbol into their flesh count as &quot;presenting&quot; it in any real sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:00:43-07:00","id":490609,"title":"","content":"Being tattooed is not even in the same dimension as presenting a religious icon forcefully. I absolutely wouldn't allow it in a serious game. You want to play a Dude's of Legend style game then that's another story entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:15:45-07:00","id":490626,"title":"","content":"What about branding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:21:10-07:00","id":490631,"title":"","content":"OK, for something a bit different, imagine a tatoo with an ink containing silver powder/liquid silver. It doesn't deal damage, but hurts like hell and leaves the skin scorched.<br /> <br /> But strictly speaking, is it abusive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:25:23-07:00","id":490633,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't allow that either. It's still a static mark on your body, not a focus for faith which is implied by the term &quot;aggressively brandishing&quot; a religious symbol. It doesn't actually matter if the person brandishing the symbol has any actual faith, just that the wolf blooded sees another person presenting the icon in such a manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:18:14-07:00","id":490735,"title":"","content":"OK, moving away from what is obviously not a unanimous idea: does the Anger Issues tell guarantee 100% that one enters Basu-Im, or does it allow a Resolve+Composure check while in Wasu-Im ?<br /> <br /> (Yes, I'm trying to find a legit/valid reason for a wolf-blooded to access Dalu form semi-reliably.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:02:39-07:00","id":490767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=490735#post490735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, moving away from what is obviously not a unanimous idea: does the Anger Issues tell guarantee 100% that one enters Basu-Im, or does it allow a Resolve+Composure check while in Wasu-Im ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it doesn't say otherwise, I'd assume it uses the normal rules for Kuruth, meaning in Wasu-Im you can use your action to roll Resolve + Composure to gain a turn of lucidity per success. An exceptional success ends the rage, but a failure sends them straight to Basu-Im. I'd also allow a Wolf-Blooded with Anger Issues to benefit from a Chain Rage Talisman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-24-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:23:37-07:00","id":490799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=490767#post490767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it doesn't say otherwise, I'd assume it uses the normal rules for Kuruth, meaning in Wasu-Im you can use your action to roll Resolve + Composure to gain a turn of lucidity per success. An exceptional success ends the rage, but a failure sends them straight to Basu-Im. I'd also allow a Wolf-Blooded with Anger Issues to benefit from a Chain Rage Talisman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Where is the &quot;Chain Rage Talisman&quot;. (God, I sound like such a newbie. I didn't even know there were magic items in werewolf.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:27:49-07:00","id":490802,"title":"","content":"There's fetishes and talens after rites, but Chain Rage is a rite that 'stores' your rage in a talisman, like a bottle or other container. It's not a magic item on its own, more of an extension of the Chain Rage rite, which is one of the first rites listed in the rite section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:37:42-07:00","id":490806,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like Nofather said, it's described in the Chain Rage rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:47:24-07:00","id":490814,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I was AFB.<br /> <br /> Thank you for answering all those questions! You are all wonderfully devoted forum goers and I am grateful for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T08:19:43-07:00","id":491661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=490735#post490735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yes, I'm trying to find a legit/valid reason for a wolf-blooded to access Dalu form semi-reliably.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He remains in Dalu .. and enjoys the physical benefits granted. Brandishing crosses or even offering the Wolf-Blooded a religious pamphlet is enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=489360#post489360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Tosses packmate a cross* &quot;Here, brandish this at me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This all seems like a reasonable scenario. As many people have pointed out, Dalu causes Lunacy, so it's not an all-good thing. I don't see any reason why someone who realizes that this happens to them wouldn't have learned to make use of it. I can see that maybe they wouldn't have figured that out, but I wouldn't say that's the case for every Wolf-Blooded with the Devil Inside.<br /> The tattoo idea wouldn't work because it would only throw him into Dalu while he was getting it. Maybe you could rule that he could wear a cross necklace and brandish it at himself, but I like Elfive's take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T08:30:12-07:00","id":491666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=491661#post491661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;He remains in Dalu .. and enjoys the physical benefits granted. Brandishing crosses or even offering the Wolf-Blooded a religious pamphlet is enough.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You left out the sentence just before that, where it says &quot;exposure to prominent religious iconography when it's presented forcefully to or at the Wolf-Blooded causes him to shift into Dalu form.&quot; Yes, a pamphlet works, but only when it's being offered to him forcefully. &quot;Take this! You need to be saved!&quot; Not, &quot;quick, use this to go Dalu!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-25-2015, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:50:11-07:00","id":491935,"title":"","content":"This seems somewhat appropriate<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-J9VEBREa68\" data-code=\"-J9VEBREa68\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-J9VEBREa68/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T06:28:32-07:00","id":492555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=491666#post491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You left out the sentence just before that, where it says &quot;exposure to prominent religious iconography when it's presented forcefully to or at the Wolf-Blooded causes him to shift into Dalu form.&quot; Yes, a pamphlet works, but only when it's being offered to him forcefully.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're playing Werewolf. Everything we do is forceful. <br /> I left the wording I did because it points out, despite the stipulation of force, that Dalu's benefits may be enjoyed and that it doesn't necessarily have to be a big deal. Themetically, the idea is that having faith shoved in your face makes &quot;the devil&quot; come out, but I see no reason why a person couldn't realize a pattern in their lives and make use of it.<br /> None of the other Tells is entirely a down-side. Even Host-Ache, which is just pain, lets you and the pack know when the host is near. If Devil Inside only let you use Dalu form in random situations where you didn't want to use it, it would be entirely a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T06:54:13-07:00","id":492558,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I vote for the version that somebody would actually choose to play a character with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T07:27:40-07:00","id":492569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=492555#post492555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're playing Werewolf. Everything we do is forceful. <br /> I left the wording I did because it points out, despite the stipulation of force, that Dalu's benefits may be enjoyed and that it doesn't necessarily have to be a big deal. Themetically, the idea is that having faith shoved in your face makes &amp;quot;the devil&amp;quot; come out, but I see no reason why a person couldn't realize a pattern in their lives and make use of it.<br /> None of the other Tells is entirely a down-side. Even Host-Ache, which is just pain, lets you and the pack know when the host is near. If Devil Inside only let you use Dalu form in random situations where you didn't want to use it, it would be entirely a drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that as entirely drawback, but eh, do what works for your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T08:33:11-07:00","id":492595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=492569#post492569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that as entirely drawback, but eh, do what works for your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd really like to hear your take on Devil Inside - as - positive is if it's not something the character can ever call upon at will. I, personally, don't see it as interesting to say &quot;no you can never use this aspect of your character on purpose&quot;, but if you can see that as enhancing to the story I'd love to have my perspective broadened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T08:50:11-07:00","id":492608,"title":"","content":"Well, apart from the fact that having unfortunate things happen to your character can be dramatically interesting and fun, it gives you a way to access Dalu form. Whether or not you can personally control it, that's mostly upside in my book. It does depend on the situation of course, but any ST worth their salt will give the player opportunities to be a badass with it, as well as using it to complicate the character's life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T14:59:48-07:00","id":492938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=492595#post492595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, don't see it as interesting to say &quot;no you can never use this aspect of your character on purpose&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The other Tell that gives you access to Dalu form is literally expressed as &quot;you have a Death Rage trigger.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:29:15-07:00","id":495129,"title":"","content":"I'd say going back to a previous point, personally if it happened in a game (though I would never subject a character to this as a GM without player consent and discussion) that this hypothetical character was branded with a religious symbol by a person of the same faith as a sort of inquisitory kind of thing, I'd have them go Dalu for the scene in which it happens only. Once out of the scene the effect is no longer there...<br /> Though I do think it'd be fitting for some Dark Age campaign where an Inquisitor brands this person and they go all Dalu, which has the Inquisitor taking this as proof the character is some kind of demonic monster... But then bad things are gonna happen and it's such an extreme case.<br /> <br /> Thats my opinion anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T14:23:29-07:00","id":495192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/489160-devil-inside-tell-unlimited-access-to-dalu-form?p=491666#post491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You left out the sentence just before that, where it says &quot;exposure to prominent religious iconography when it's presented forcefully to or at the Wolf-Blooded causes him to shift into Dalu form.&quot; Yes, a pamphlet works, but only when it's being offered to him forcefully. &quot;Take this! You need to be saved!&quot; Not, &quot;quick, use this to go Dalu!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you just made that make sense to me... I kept thinking &quot;those poor Jehovah's Witnesses&quot; most of them don't deserve that... and it would allow a wolfblooded go to church just fine too. Its when someone is throwing it in their face that it sets them off... that poor street preacher...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:46:43-07:00","id":498788,"title":"","content":"About the Anger Issues Tell (again):<br /> <br /> Could the specific <i>Kuruth Trigger</i> be such that one could want to trigger it <b>on purpose</b>? Like risking a barbarian/berserker rage purposefully entering a dangerous frenzy where s/he loses control of her/him/self to better fight off threats ? Does the specific trigger need to be only involuntary ?<br /> <br /> The way I see it, if &quot;facing the threat of death&quot; is the specific trigger (which wouldn't activate when not threatened by lethal damage, let's say), could you still willingly enter Wasu-Im to get the benefits at the risk of ending up in a Basu-Im rampage?<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Does the transformation happen as an Instant action or Reflexively ? I'd be inclined to say that since a Kuruth Trigger makes the character \u00abshift[] immediately into [...] Dalu form and remain[] in that form for the duration\u00bb, this would be Reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-01-2015, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}